# 📘 Two Traders: One Mistake, One Method

By Veer Shinde

The book's title points to a powerful lesson about trading: two traders can face the same market, make different decisions, and get very different results. The difference often comes down to their process, risk management, discipline and response to mistakes.

A useful way to approach this book is to focus on building a repeatable trading method rather than chasing profits or trying to predict every market movement.

## 1. The central story: Rick vs Carl

The book follows two contrasting traders, Rick and Carl, whose experiences illustrate the difference between emotional trading and disciplined trading.&#x20;

