1\. FOMO — Fear of missing out

Seeing a stock rise rapidly can make you feel that you must buy immediately. But entering without a plan can expose you to unnecessary risk.

Action: If you miss a trade, let it go. Another opportunity may come.

[How to Read a Trading Journal (and Use It to Improve) | For Traders](https://images.openai.com/static-rsc-4/u4FT7EkCwR7LeG5bXxPmKxsTrZOZ3Qp_lekodKIGtfivi6tJ_nXfr6rsIKpieWEiFq563ZF4CTMaoPjq1DlGT3-67_Vk0FsrFfVY36FVy3Z6JmT882zwRl4GQMey_pH8uJW7gSKHkxBNJhDJAh0Ildw4bfr4Ji0wCG_FykHSnhU?purpose=inline)

2\. Revenge trading

After losing money, a trader may take another trade simply to recover the loss. This often leads to rushed decisions.

Action: After a significant mistake, stop trading, review what happened and return only when you can follow your rules.

