## 3. Use this pre-trade checklist

Before every simulated trade, answer these questions:

Does this trade match my predefined setup?

Can I explain the reason for entering?

Have I identified my exit and invalidation point?

Is the planned risk acceptable?

Am I calm rather than chasing a move or recovering a loss?

0 of 5 checks completed. If any answer is no, pause and reassess.

## 4. Track what actually matters

At the end of each week, review these five measures:

| Measure               | What to examine                          |
| --------------------- | ---------------------------------------- |
| Rule adherence        | Did you follow your written plan?        |
| FOMO incidents        | How often did you chase a move?          |
| Revenge-trading urges | Did you act on the urge or resist it?    |
| Risk discipline       | Did you respect planned risk limits?     |
| Emotional control     | Could you accept uncertainty and losses? |

Don't judge your progress by profit alone. A simulated winning trade made by breaking your rules can reinforce a bad habit; a losing trade taken correctly can still be a good decision.

